y above FY2026 GAAP operating margin (4.7%) + D&A \u2014 no structural recovery.\n4. Operating leases of $3.1B are real claims on FCF; the company is not balance-sheet strong.\n5. E-commerce growth is decelerating; Macy's is losing to off-price and specialty retailers structurally.\n6. The stock is not a \"value\" stock \u2014 it is a \"value trap\": median analyst target is $23, just 0.8% above market.\n7. Short interest at 13% is high; a squeeze is the only reason to own this.\n\n**Logic combat score:**\n- Long score: 6/10\n- Short score: 7/10  \nGap = 1 \u2014 within noise. Conviction should not exceed Medium.\n\n**Adversarial data:** No Hindenburg report found on Macy's; industry sources (Morningstar) rate \"No Moat\" [Estimate].\n\n**Killed arguments:**\n- \"Real estate value > market cap\": dismissed for base case because management has not executed major monetization; only if a large sale-leaseback or entity sale is announced would we move it to a scenario.\n- \"Saks bankruptcy = permanent share gain\": valid only if Bloomingdale's can hold comps >5% for >2 years; otherwise it is a one-off.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 10. Audit Results\n\n**A. Methodology Audit:** \u2713 Engine 2 selected; no DCF-only, no peer-only, no TAM-only.\n**B. Valuation Audit:** \u2713 Cross-checked DCF vs mid-cycle P/E vs EV/EBITDA vs P/B. Sensitivity table provided.\n**C. Bias Audit:** \u26a0\ufe0f Overconfidence risk \u2014 success probability in base case (50%) is above retail turnaround base rate (~30%). We added a \"base-rate shock\" check and kept bull case at 20%.\n**D. Consistency Audit:** \u2713 Tags applied; time points consistent (T0 = Aug 2026). No mixing of FY2026 actual with FY2027 guidance without labels.\n**E. Narrative Audit:** \u2713 \"Turnaround\" narrative is quantified via comps, margin, and FCF thresholds.\n**F. Red Team Audit:** \u2713 Section 9 completed; logic gap small.\n**G. Data Integrity Audit:** \u26a0\ufe0f Capex discrepancy unresolved (PP&E vs incl. software)