M concurrently (correlation \u2192 1 in stress).\n- Tail correlation: M behaved like the market in 2020 (severe) and 2022 (moderate);\n  its idiosyncratic tail is a 2008-style consumer shock.\n- Conditional VaR (95%): $10\u201312/share within 12 months [Assumption \u2014 based on the\n  COVID trough and 52-week low $11.77].\n- The 13% short interest is a portfolio hedge: a market-driven rally triggers short\n  covering, adding positive skew to the position.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550 SECTION 8 \u2014 MONITORING RULES & THESIS INTEGRITY \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nThesis KPI thresholds (any breach \u2192 re-evaluate the thesis within 10 days):\n| KPI | Threshold | Breach trigger |\n|---|---|---|\n| Go-forward comp (O+L+M) | \u2265 +1.0% per quarter | <0% for 2 consecutive quarters |\n| Adjusted EBITDA margin | FY2027 \u2265 7.5%; FY2028 \u2265 8.0% | <7.0% (any quarter) |\n| Gross margin ex-tariff | Stable \u2265 38.5% [Actual Q1: 38.9% ex-tariff = 38.6%] | Erosion >100bps/yr |\n| Total debt | \u2264 $2.5B | >$3.0B or ABL draws |\n| FCF (ex-SBC) | \u2265 $0.65B annually | <$0.50B |\n| Inventory | Change \u2264 \u00b15% YoY | >8% build vs flat/declining comps |\n| Dividend | Maintained at $0.1915/qtr | Cut = severe signal |\n\nStep 7-4 Pre-Mortem: see Section 7 (A/B/C) \u2014 early warnings are integrated above.\nStep 7-5 Decision Journal Entry: see Section 11.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550 SECTION 9 \u2014 RED TEAM / ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n9-1. SHORT THESIS (same data set):\n1. Macy's 40.3% share is of a SHRINKING pie: online and off-price have taken the growth;\n   store-based department stores have lost share every year for a decade [Estimate].\n2. Four positive comp quarters are flattered by the closure base: total revenue is flat\n   to down; FY2027 guidance (+0.5% to +1.2% comp) implies real (unit) growth \u2248 0.\n3. Tariffs are a margin tax: average apparel tariff 35.1% [Estimate]; the company only\n   offset 30bps in Q1 FY2027; guidance assumes H2 relief that is not guaranteed.\n4. Economic leverage is the real story: $3.1B operating leases + $2.4B debt \u2248 $5.5B of\n   fixed obligations; adjusted net-debt/EBITDA \u2248 2.9\u00d7 when leases are counted [Arithmetic].\n5. The \"turnaround\" is a re-run of Polaris (2020) \u2014 which failed to stop the 2020\n   collapse; management has not yet guided EBITDA margin ABOVE the 7.9% held flat.\n6. July retail sales \u22120.6% m/m [Actual] is the first crack in the consumer; Macy's is a\n   pure-proxy short for the late-cycle consumer.\n7. Index/passive vulnerability: 99.4% institutional ownership; if M exits a major index,\n   forced selling amplifies downside.\n8. Insider ownership 1.5%: management participates in upside via SBC but has no\n   meaningful downside exposure.\n\n9-2. LOGIC COMBAT:\n- Long logic: 6/10 (balance sheet, FCF yield, evidence of positive execution, optionality).\n- Short logic: 5/10 (structural decline, tariff burden, consumer risk, lease burden).\n- Gap = 1 (<2) \u2192 conviction must stay capped at MEDIUM. Already applied.\n\n9-3. ADVERSARIAL DATA: no active Hindenburg-style report found [Unconfirmed]; activist\npressure is present (strategic-options discussions reported) [Estimate \u2014 research pack].\n\n9-4. KILLED ARGUMENTS (and revive conditions):\n- \"Real estate ($6B dark value) fully backstops the stock\" \u2014 KILLED: liquidation would\n  destroy the EBITDA that underpins any going-concern value; cap rates on mall-anchor\n  boxes are punitive post-2020. REVIVE: if an activist wins a board seat and announces a\n  sale-leaseback JV with realized proceeds >$3B.\n- \"The market is pricing bankruptcy\" \u2014 KILLED: no maturities until 2030, $2B ABL, OCF\n  positive even in the COVID trough ($0.649B FY2021) [Actual]. REVIVE: ABL drawn >$1B\n  AND go-forward comps <\u22123%.\n- \"Tariffs are a one-off 2025 event\" \u2014 KILLED by evidence (Dec-2025 tariff rate 35.1%\n  [Estimate]; FY2027 guidance still assumes H2 improvement). REVIVE only with actual\n  refunds collected (>$100M) and tariff rollback.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550 SECTION 10 \u2014 AUDIT RESULTS (MANDATORY) \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nA. Methodology Audit: PASS\n- Engine 2 selected for Cyclical/Turnaround; transition criteria >80% met; DCF is NOT the\n  sole conclusion; no peer-multiple-only conclusion; no TAM narrative; macro included.\nB. Valuation Audit: PASS (with disclosed sensitivities)\n- WACC fully derived; terminal value = 7.79/11.06 = 70% of EV [Arithmetic] \u2014 disclosed;\n  tornado sensitivity provided; debt-definition sensitivity provided ($11.9/sh);\n  balance-sheet time-points aligned to FY2026A; no mixing of RE gains into forward ops.\nC. Bias Audit: PASS WITH WARNING\n- The 5-beat streak creates anchoring risk; base-rate discipline imposed a 35% bear\n  probability; success-probability was 65% raw, capped to 65% but the 2\u00d7 base-rate\n  red flag was explicitly acknowledged and priced.\nD. Consistency Audit: PASS\n- FY2026A (ended Jan-2026) vs Macy's-labeled FY2026 guidance (year ending Jan-2027)\n  explicitly distinguished; GAAP vs adjusted net income kept separate; adjusted EBITDA\n  excludes RE gains per the revised non-GAAP definition [Actual].\nE. Narrative Audit: PASS\n- \"Bold New Chapter\" management claims tested against 4 quarters of comps; LT company\n  targets treated as assumptions, not facts; guidance accepted only through